5 in East Lansing, Michigan, stands as one of the foremost public research universities in the United States. As the first institution of higher education in the U.S. to teach agricultural science, it played a pivotal role in the development of land-grant colleges, a system instituted by the Morrill Act of 1862, which aimed to promote higher education in agriculture, science, and engineering. This initiative was driven by the vision of key figures such as Justin Morrill, who sought to provide practical education to the masses, making higher education accessible to a broader demographic and laying the groundwork for future educational reforms.

